vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the inventory investigation to a subagent while I look at the rest.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\n`python3 -m unittest` now passes all 16 tests. Before the fixes it ran 15: `tests/test_search.py` couldn't be imported, so its two tests were counted as one error. I didn't change any tests. I tracked the work with the todo list tool, and a subagent investigated `test_inventory.py`.\n\nFixes in `catalog/`:\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` left the year as a string, so `age()` crashed when subtracting it. It now converts the year with `int(year)`.\n- **`factory.py`**: added the missing third sample book, `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`.\n- **`fees.py`**: the fee was `days_late + DAILY_FEE`; it's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent()` had an off-by-one slice (`[-n - 1:]`) that returned one event too many. The subagent found this. It's now `[-n:] if n > 0 else []`. The `n > 0` check is a small addition no test asks for: without it, `recent(0)` would return the whole history.\n- **`members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment above it and the tests both say 5. Changed it to 5.\n- **`search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`; it now imports it from `catalog.text`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 89545, "requests_cache_write": 58371, "requests_cost_usd": 0.379224, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 3469, "reread": false, "rule_or